			<div class="content" id="post-content-1593875">
									

<p>Certainly bizarre. I rather like the memetic aspect, in particular the reveal about how, when I looked at the photo, I could only see Luna-2 in the image because it was circled.</p>
<p>However I admit I am confused as to whether persons perceiving the change in sea level are actually affecting the sea level for everyone else. I'm assuming not, which means this thing is Keter because of its potential to massively change life on Earth if enough people know about it to point it out to everyone else. Effectively, Luna-2 messes things up just by existing in the minds of enough people, so containment hinges on it not existing. Yea, I like that.</p>
<p>It's a bit long, though. The impeded movement/swimming through air is a bit overboard, especially the implication that the medium is thicker than water. If it's mostly tides that are altered, wouldn't it just be sea water? I like the drowning and the bit about the boat in the recovery is great, but I think the article could stand a bit of trimming.</p>

